# Template for the .env file at the repository root, which Docker Compose reads for
# docker-compose.yml. Copy it, make the copy readable by your user only, then set the two
# passwords:
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it, and never put real passwords in this template.

# --- Docker Compose (instruction 3) -------------------------------------------------------------

# Required: every `docker compose` command for this project (even ps, logs and down) fails until
# both are set. Generate each one with
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# and paste it unquoted. Use letters and digits only, as hex is: Compose reads a $ in a value as
# a variable and an unquoted " #" as a comment, so either can silently shorten the password, and
# Redis takes its password as a single word, so a space stops Redis (which then prints the
# password in its log). Hex also needs no escaping in connection URLs.
# PostgreSQL takes its password only when its data volume is first created; to change it later,
# also change it inside PostgreSQL (infra/README.md shows how) or start again with an empty
# volume. For a new Redis password, run `docker compose up -d`: it recreates the container,
# whose config file then holds the new password.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
REDIS_PASSWORD=

# Optional: uncomment a line to change its default.

# PostgreSQL superuser and database name. Like the password, they apply only when the data volume
# is first created, but the health check uses them every time: change them only together with a
# new, empty volume, or PostgreSQL logs a FATAL line for every check (see infra/README.md).
# POSTGRES_USER=postgres
# POSTGRES_DB=apex_garage

# Host ports, always bound to 127.0.0.1. Change one if the port is taken, for example by a
# PostgreSQL or Redis server installed directly on this machine.
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# REDIS_PORT=6379

# To run a second, separate copy of these services (its own containers and volumes) next to the
# first, give it another project name and other ports.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=apex-garage
